    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["Q1", "Q2", "C3"],
      "pins": ["Q1.1", "Q1.2", "Q2.3", "C3.1", "C3.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(Q1-G)", "VCC"],
      "observed": "The P-MOSFET gate net Net-(Q1-G) contains only C3.2, Q1.1 and Q2.3. C3 is a 100 nF capacitor from VCC to the gate, and Q2 collector is the only active path; there is no resistor from Q1 gate to Q1 source/VCC.",
      "expected": "For a high-side P-MOSFET switch driven by an NPN transistor, a DC pull-up resistor from gate to source/VCC is required so that when Q2 is off the gate returns to source and Q1 turns off. A capacitor alone cannot provide the DC pull-up.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(Q1-G) : C3.2(passive) Q1.1(G,input) Q2.3(C,passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "VCC : C1.1(passive) C3.1(passive) J5.2(Pin_2,passive) JP1.2(B,passive) Q1.2(S,passive) R6.1(passive) U1.3(VI,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Q1 | Q_PMOS_GSD | Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23 | Device:Q_PMOS_GSD | P-MOSFET transistor, gate/source/drain"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C3 VCC Net-_Q1-G_ 100n"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "When the PWM drive turns Q2 off, Q1's gate has no path to charge to VCC/source, so the PMOS may remain on; /VCC_OUT can stay energized and fan PWM/speed control will be unreliable or fail.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The board's high-side P-MOS fan power switch lacks a gate pull-up resistor; the only gate-to-VCC element is a 100 nF capacitor, which cannot reliably turn the PMOS off when the NPN driver is off."
}

